# File structure and size

Keep files focused. Prefer extraction when a file grows past soft limits; do not split tiny modules for purity.

## Soft limits (source, not tests)

| Layer | Target | Extract when |
|-------|--------|--------------|
| `apps/*/src/App.tsx` | **≤ 80 lines** | Screen logic → `hooks/`, JSX blocks → `components/` |
| `apps/*/src/components/*.tsx` | **≤ 120 lines** | Sub-sections or repeated markup |
| `apps/*/src/hooks/*.ts` | **≤ 150 lines** | Split by domain (auth vs feature) |
| `packages/api-client/src/*.ts` | **≤ 150 lines** | One module per domain (`auth`, `quickbooks`, `errors`) |
| `packages/ui/src/**` | **≤ 120 lines** | Already shared; keep components small |
| `backend/app/Http/Controllers/**` | **≤ 115 lines** | Move logic to services (Pest Arch enforces `< 116`) |
| `backend/app/Services/**` | **≤ 250 lines** | Split only when mixing unrelated domains (OAuth vs CRUD) |

Test files may exceed these limits; split test suites by feature when navigation becomes painful (~400+ lines).

## Extraction patterns (React apps)

```
apps/<app>/src/
  App.tsx              # Composition root only: auth gate + layout + one feature import
  hooks/               # Feature state and API orchestration (no JSX)
  components/          # Presentational UI for this app (props in, events out)
```

- **`App.tsx`**: loading → login → dashboard routing; no business handlers beyond wiring.
- **Hooks**: call `@ellr/api-client`, own local state, return data + handlers.
- **Components**: receive props; no direct `apiFetch` or `@ellr/api-client` imports unless the component is a dedicated data container (avoid by default).

Reuse `@ellr/ui` for cross-app pieces (auth, layout, alerts). Keep app-specific screens in `apps/*/src/components/`.

## Extraction patterns (backend)

```
app/Http/Controllers/Api/   # Thin JSON orchestration (≤ 115 lines; Pest Arch < 116)
app/Http/Requests/          # Validation rules per endpoint or resource
app/Services/               # Business logic and QBO SDK access (≤ ~250 lines)
```

- **Controllers**: one resource or domain per class (`AuthController`, `QboEmployeeController`, `QuickBooksAuthController`, `TimeActivityController`). Validate via Form Requests; delegate to services.
- **Services**: one primary domain per class. Extract when mixing unrelated concerns (e.g. employee authorization vs time-activity CRUD).
- **Token resolution**: `QuickBooksTokenResolverService::resolve(User $user)`; controllers pass `$request->user()` (not `auth()->user()`, for static analysis). Inject `Request` on actions that do not already use a Form Request.
- Extract a new service only when responsibilities are clearly separate, not for every private method.

## API controllers at the Pest Arch line limit

Pest Arch enforces **`< 116` lines** per `App\Http\Controllers\Api` class (see `tests/Arch/ArchitectureTest.php`). PHPDoc on every public method counts toward that budget.

A **full CRUD** controller (5 actions) with Form Requests and QBO token resolution often lands at **~115 lines** with no room for a private `userAndToken()` helper (~+10 lines). **Option A (project default):** keep inline `$user = $request->user();` + `$token = $this->tokenResolver->resolve($user);` in each action. Do **not** add a private helper just to dedupe those two lines if it would fail `composer test:arch`.

To regain headroom (private helper or more actions), **raise the Pest Arch limit and `file-structure.mdc` together** in one change; do not ping-pong between helper and inline across PRs.

Reference: `TimeActivityController` (5 actions, inline user + token).

## When NOT to extract

- A private controller helper whose only job is `$request->user()` + `tokenResolver->resolve($user)` on a **5-action CRUD** class already at ~115 lines (see **API controllers at the Pest Arch line limit** in `file-structure.mdc`).
- A helper used once in the same file (< 10 lines).
- A third React app does not exist yet: do not premature-split `api.ts` unless it crosses 200 lines or mixes unrelated domains.
- "One function per file" micro-modules.

## PR checklist

- [ ] `App.tsx` and new controllers stay under soft limits (Pest Arch + PHPMD where applicable).
- [ ] New feature logic lives in a hook or service, not copied into `App.tsx`.
- [ ] Shared behavior moved to `packages/*`, not duplicated between admin and timesheet.
- [ ] `composer test:arch`, `npm run lint:deps`, and `npm run lint:dup` pass.
- [ ] Tests updated; behavior unchanged unless intentionally fixed.

## Automated enforcement

| Tool | Command | When |
|------|---------|------|
| Pest Arch | `composer test:arch` | pre-push |
| PHPMD | `composer phpmd` (via `composer lint`) | pre-commit |
| dependency-cruiser | `npm run lint:deps` | pre-push |
| jscpd (source) | `npm run lint:dup` (max 5 % duplicated lines) | pre-push |
| jscpd (tests) | `npm run lint:dup:tests` (max 12 %; higher min block size) | pre-push |
